=== start ===
I was just walking in from the fields. I had my holiday clothes on, ready for the evening feast.
Then the centurion’s spear tapped my shoulder. No choice. No argument. They forced me to pick up the wet timber.
The wood was rough—splinters tearing into my chest, the blood from his back soaking right into my tunic.
* [Did he speak to you while you carried it?] -> speech
* [How did the crowd react along the path?] -> mob

=== speech ===
He could barely breathe. He just looked at me once. There were no words, but the weight of that look was heavier than the timber.
-> closing

=== mob ===
Some were throwing rocks, others were weeping. The soldiers just kept pushing us forward with horsewhips. It was a nightmare.
-> closing

=== closing ===
-> DONE